'''''Aichryson santamariensis''''' is a species of plant endemic to the island of [[Santa Maria Island|Santa Maria]] in the [[Azores]]. This species was previously part of the similar ''[[Aichryson villosum]]'', restricted now only to the neighboring [[Madeira]].<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Moura |first1=Mónica |last2=Carine |first2=Mark |last3=Menezes de Sequeira |first3=Miguel |title=Aichryson santamariensis (Crassulaceae): a new species endemic to Santa Maria in the Azores |journal=Phytotaxa |date=11 November 2015 |volume=234 |issue=1 |pages=37 |doi=10.11646/phytotaxa.234.1.2 |url=https://www.biotaxa.org/Phytotaxa/article/view/phytotaxa.234.1.2 |access-date=24 February 2022|url-access=subscription }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=World Plants: Complete Plant List |url=https://www.worldplants.de/world-plants-complete-list/complete-plant-list/?name=Aichryson-santamariensis#g- |website=www.worldplants.de |access-date=24 February 2022}}</ref>

